  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">HCFC Phase-out Management Plan, Stage II</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Preparation of Stage-II HCFC Phase-out Management Plan (stage II) Preparation phase: BFA/PHA/84/PRP/  The Executive Committee of the Multilateral Fund for the Implementation of the Montreal Protocol, at its 62nd Meeting, approved stage I of the HCFC phase-out management plan (HPMP) for Burkina Faso to achieve the 35% reduction in HCFC consumption by 2020, at the amount of  US $580,000 plus agency support cost of US $75,400 for UNEP as the lead agency and US $500,000 plus agency support costs of US $37,500 for UNIDO as the cooperating agency.</narrative>
  </description>
